 "MATH_0011": "$S$", "MATH_0012": "$S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-definition-morphism-coverings}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{topologies-definition-zariski-covering}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-pullback-family}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-Zariski-refinement-coverings-equivalence}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 2, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5e8e0f2fed2a357f845065c248e1bec477385026a702aee664ad507ad641926a", "source_math_skeleton_hash": "sha256:f48831763168f30c2741aebcc7c7328f0ed60aa2e3aa3b3ec4ec9e0db82db5dd", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d84680467f83bbdc5c27e2d43dda3020885bdc62fe2c30d1fd2e8e5b5af70cd3", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002>, and\n<MATH_0003>,\nbe families of morphisms with target <MATH_0004>.\nLet <MATH_0005>, <MATH_0006> and\n<MATH_0007> be a morphism of families\nof maps with fixed target, see\nSites, Definition <REF_0001>.\nAssume that for each <MATH_0008> the family\n<MATH_0009> is a Zariski covering (see\nTopologies, Definition <REF_0002>)\nof <MATH_0010>. Then the pullback functor\n<MATHSEG_0001>descent data relative to <MATHSEG_0002>descent data relative to <MATHSEG_0003>\nof Lemma <REF_0003> is an equivalence of categories.\nIn particular, the category of schemes over <MATH_0011>\nis equivalent to the category\nof descent data relative to any Zariski covering of <MATH_0012>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bee91e0e0898ee28cb3340badd0f299bba9988d0193b61b45998e9ca96ad28d6", "unit_id": "tag:02VY:statement"}
