datum <MATH_0010>\nrelative to the Zariski covering\n<MATH_0011>.\nNote that <MATH_0012> is an isomorphism from the open\n<MATH_0013> of <MATH_0014> to the corresponding\nopen of <MATH_0015>. It follows from\nSchemes, Section <REF_0002>\nthat we may glue <MATH_0016> into a scheme\n<MATH_0017> over <MATH_0018>. Moreover, the morphisms <MATH_0019>\nfor <MATH_0020> and <MATH_0021> glue to a morphism\n<MATH_0022>\nsatisfying the cocycle condition (details omitted).\nHence we obtain the desired descent datum\n<MATH_0023> relative to <MATH_0024>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:547ef0c26cf8ec4650587a4f4e1cdfafe3ebe6c92c71c22af5cf8db203514e64", "unit_id": "tag:02VY:proof"}
